1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,252
Two Hands.

2
00:00:01,302 --> 00:00:04,290
Verifiable quality control for handwritten numbers.

3
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:07,761
For the institutes that run Mexico's counts,

4
00:00:07,811 --> 00:00:09,497
and their auditors:

5
00:00:09,547 --> 00:00:11,667
OCR reads the number.

6
00:00:11,717 --> 00:00:15,573
Two Hands checks whether the whole form agrees.

7
00:00:15,623 --> 00:00:18,610
Here, the official record typed 480.

8
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:20,780
The paper says 180.

9
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:22,950
Gemma read the paper.

10
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,227
Mexico counts every tally sheet twice:

11
00:00:26,277 --> 00:00:30,439
a fast preliminary capture, then the certified count.

12
00:00:30,489 --> 00:00:34,652
On 6.5% of the polling stations not recounted,

13
00:00:34,702 --> 00:00:39,333
the two official records of the same paper disagree.

14
00:00:39,383 --> 00:00:44,950
A sum says something is wrong; the photo says which field.

15
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,550
Gemma, on AMD, reads every field twice:

16
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:52,150
the digits and the amount in words.

17
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:55,750
The referee is the paper's own arithmetic.

18
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:58,000
Every check holds: accepted.

19
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:02,950
One fails: a person sees the field, with its photo.

20
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,839
Here is a real sheet.

21
00:01:05,889 --> 00:01:11,617
Gemma misread one field as 23, in digits and in words.

22
00:01:11,667 --> 00:01:14,987
The paper's own arithmetic catches it:

23
00:01:15,037 --> 00:01:19,802
the rows sum to 366, not the 466 total.

24
00:01:19,852 --> 00:01:26,543
So it is not accepted: it goes to a person, with the photo.

25
00:01:26,593 --> 00:01:28,950
The paper says 123.

26
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,807
Every field gets a receipt.

27
00:01:31,857 --> 00:01:35,617
Verified: it proves the record is unchanged.

28
00:01:35,667 --> 00:01:38,950
Not that the reading is right.

29
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,236
Now a live read.

30
00:01:41,286 --> 00:01:45,807
One request to Gemma, on the AMD Token Factory.

31
00:01:45,857 --> 00:01:50,379
We cut the wait; the timer stays on screen.

32
00:01:50,429 --> 00:01:52,664
It took 90 seconds.

33
00:01:52,714 --> 00:01:54,950
Every check holds: accepted.

34
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,245
This is the product.

35
00:01:57,295 --> 00:02:01,835
An auditor brings the typed data and the scans.

36
00:02:01,885 --> 00:02:06,884
Here, the sample: 6,000 fields, from the stored AMD reads,

37
00:02:06,934 --> 00:02:08,720
checked in seconds.

38
00:02:08,770 --> 00:02:11,016
267 disputes, strongest first.

39
00:02:11,066 --> 00:02:16,065
This one: the capture keyed 75; the paper says 175.

40
00:02:16,115 --> 00:02:19,278
One fingerprint seals the whole report.

41
00:02:19,328 --> 00:02:22,950
Change one number, and the check fails.

42
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,330
The proof.

43
00:02:24,380 --> 00:02:28,930
Gemma on AMD read 1,270 real handwritten tally sheets.

44
00:02:28,980 --> 00:02:33,070
49 capture errors, confirmed by the certified count.

45
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:38,130
Recall: 27 of 28 capture errors the certified count reveals,

46
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:40,430
in one state, pre-registered.

47
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:44,110
A person re-read the AI-judged disputes blind:

48
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:45,950
0 read differently.

49
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:51,355
On Baja California Sur's local actas: 91.6% field match.

50
00:02:51,405 --> 00:02:56,220
The Google Document AI reading the state bought

51
00:02:56,270 --> 00:02:57,842
scored 62.84%.

52
00:02:57,892 --> 00:03:02,707
Same per-field metric: theirs on all 2,020 actas,

53
00:03:02,757 --> 00:03:05,950
ours on a random 300.

54
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,379
Same 300 forms, same gate.

55
00:03:09,429 --> 00:03:13,950
It accepts 1.8x the forms Qwen does,

56
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,807
4.6x cheaper, 2.8x faster.

57
00:03:16,857 --> 00:03:19,664
A whole state: Colima.

58
00:03:19,714 --> 00:03:25,950
Gemma on AMD read all 982 sheets for 14 cents.

59
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:30,041
Each strong finding becomes a case in Evolus.

60
00:03:30,091 --> 00:03:35,041
The agent runs on Gemma, on AMD, and drafts it.

61
00:03:35,091 --> 00:03:39,132
A script, not the model, scores the evidence.

62
00:03:39,182 --> 00:03:40,950
The auditor decides.

63
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,903
Where it breaks.

64
00:03:42,953 --> 00:03:46,810
The first gate had a blind spot:

65
00:03:46,860 --> 00:03:51,206
on fresh forms it would have accepted 3114

66
00:03:51,256 --> 00:03:54,136
where the paper says 314.

67
00:03:54,186 --> 00:03:59,020
Gate version two, fixed before those forms were drawn,

68
00:03:59,070 --> 00:04:01,950
sent it to a person.

69
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:08,108
The auditor looks at 4% of the fields, each with its photo.

70
00:04:08,158 --> 00:04:13,792
On 6 June 2027, 32 local elections join the federal midterm.

71
00:04:13,842 --> 00:04:16,634
$1 per sheet audited, proposed:

72
00:04:16,684 --> 00:04:23,266
for Morelos, half a percent of what it paid to run its count.

73
00:04:23,316 --> 00:04:28,950
The first step: a paid shadow-mode pilot on one state's count.

74
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:33,117
Every number re-derives from public data, with one command.

75
00:04:33,167 --> 00:04:34,367
Two Hands.

76
00:04:34,417 --> 00:04:37,283
Verifiable quality control for handwritten numbers.

77
00:04:37,333 --> 00:04:38,950
Running on AMD.
